  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1219 AM CDT Sun Aug 16 2026\n\nThe hot and dry doldrums of summer will continue for the next \nseveral days as a 596dam upper-level ridge will remain the dominant \nfeature across the southern US. As the upper-level flow becomes more \nzonal across the northern tier of the US, the ridge will retrograde \nwestward by Tuesday and become centered over west Texas through \nWednesday. The warmest days look to be Tuesday and Wednesday when \n850mb temperatures will increase to 25-27 deg C and the ridge is \ndirectly overhead.  There is a medium to high (40-80%) chance for \nhigh temperatures to exceed 105 degrees across the Big Country and \nConcho Valley, so heat advisories could be needed.  High \ntemperatures will be around 100 elsewhere.\n\nFor Thursday and Friday, the ridge will shift further westward and \nbecome centered over the Four Corners region.  While temperatures \nmay be a few degrees lower, this likely will not bring much overall \nrelief from the heat for most areas.  In addition, a weak trough \naxis will move into the Southern Plains in place of the ridge.  This \nwill push a cold front southward into North Texas on Friday, which \ncould introduce some low (<20%) rain chances into Saturday for the \nBig Country.",
